.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OSSL_CMP_MSG_GET0_HEADER 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm OSSL_CMP_MSG_get0_header ,
.Nm OSSL_CMP_MSG_get_bodytype ,
.Nm OSSL_CMP_MSG_get0_certreq_publickey ,
.Nm OSSL_CMP_MSG_update_transactionID ,
.Nm OSSL_CMP_MSG_update_recipNonce ,
.Nm OSSL_CMP_CTX_setup_CRM ,
.Nm OSSL_CMP_MSG_read ,
.Nm OSSL_CMP_MSG_write ,
.Nm d2i_OSSL_CMP_MSG_bio ,
.Nm i2d_OSSL_CMP_MSG_bio
.Nd function(s) manipulating CMP messages
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/cmp.h
.Ft OSSL_CMP_PKIHEADER *
.Fo OSSL_CMP_MSG_get0_header
.Fa "const OSSL_CMP_MSG *msg"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_CMP_MSG_get_bodytype
.Fa "const OSSL_CMP_MSG *msg"
.Fc
.Ft X509_PUBKEY *
.Fo OSSL_CMP_MSG_get0_certreq_publickey
.Fa "const OSSL_CMP_MSG *msg"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_CMP_MSG_update_transactionID
.Fa "OSSL_CMP_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "OSSL_CMP_MSG *msg"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_CMP_MSG_update_recipNonce
.Fa "OSSL_CMP_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "OSSL_CMP_MSG *msg"
.Fc
.Ft OSSL_CRMF_MSG *
.Fo OSSL_CMP_CTX_setup_CRM
.Fa "OSSL_CMP_CTX *ctx"
.Fa "int for_KUR"
.Fa "int rid"
.Fc
.Ft OSSL_CMP_MSG *
.Fo OSSL_CMP_MSG_read
.Fa "const char *file"
.Fa "OSSL_LIB_CTX *libctx"
.Fa "const char *propq"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_CMP_MSG_write
.Fa "const char *file"
.Fa "const OSSL_CMP_MSG *msg"
.Fc
.Ft OSSL_CMP_MSG *
.Fo d2i_OSSL_CMP_MSG_bio
.Fa "BIO *bio"
.Fa "OSSL_CMP_MSG **msg"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo i2d_OSSL_CMP_MSG_bio
.Fa "BIO *bio"
.Fa "const OSSL_CMP_MSG *msg"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn OSSL_CMP_MSG_get0_header
returns the header of the given CMP message.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_CMP_MSG_get_bodytype
returns the body type of the given CMP message.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_CMP_MSG_get0_certreq_publickey
expects that
.Fa msg
is a certificate request message and returns the public key in its
certificate template if present.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_CMP_MSG_update_transactionID
updates the transactionID field in the header of the given message
according to the CMP_CTX. If
.Fa ctx
does not contain a transaction ID, a fresh one is created before.
The message gets re-protected (if protecting requests is required).
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_CMP_MSG_update_recipNonce
updates the recipNonce field in the header of the given message
according to the CMP_CTX. The message gets re-protected (if protecting
requests is required).
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_CMP_CTX_setup_CRM
creates a CRMF certificate request message from various information
provided in the CMP context argument
.Fa ctx
for inclusion in a CMP request message based on details contained in
.Fa ctx .
The
.Fa rid
argument defines the request identifier to use, which typically is 0.
.Pp
The subject DN included in the certificate template is the first
available value of these:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It any subject name in Fa ctx No set via Xr OSSL_CMP_CTX_set1_subjectName 3 No - if it is the NULL-DN (i.e., any empty sequence of RDNs), no subject is included,
.It the subject field of any PKCS#10 CSR set in Fa ctx No via Xr OSSL_CMP_CTX_set1_p10CSR 3 ,
.It the subject field of any reference certificate given in Fa ctx No (see Xr OSSL_CMP_CTX_set1_oldCert 3 No ), but only if Fa for_KUR No is nonzero or the Fa ctx No does not include a Subject Alternative Name.
.El
The public key included is the first available value of these:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It the public key derived from any key set via Xr OSSL_CMP_CTX_set0_newPkey 3 ,
.It the public key of any PKCS#10 CSR given in Fa ctx ,
.It the public key of any reference certificate given in Fa ctx No (see Xr OSSL_CMP_CTX_set1_oldCert 3 No ),
.It the public key derived from any client's private key set via Xr OSSL_CMP_CTX_set1_pkey 3 .
.El
The set of X.509 extensions to include is computed as follows.
If a PKCS#10 CSR is present in
.Fa ctx ,
default extensions are taken from there, otherwise the empty set is
taken as the initial value.
If there is a reference certificate in
.Fa ctx
and contains Subject Alternative Names (SANs) and
.Sy OSSL_CMP_OPT_SUBJECTALTNAME_NODEFAULT
is not set, these override any SANs from the PKCS#10 CSR. The extensions
are further augmented or overridden by any extensions with the same OIDs
included in the
.Fa ctx
via
.Xr OSSL_CMP_CTX_set0_reqExtensions 3 .
The SANs are further overridden by any SANs included in
.Fa ctx
via
.Xr OSSL_CMP_CTX_push1_subjectAltName 3 .
Finally, policies are overridden by any policies included in
.Fa ctx
via
.Xr OSSL_CMP_CTX_push0_policy 3 .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_CMP_CTX_setup_CRM
also sets the sets the regToken control
.Sy oldCertID
for KUR messages using the issuer name and serial number of the
reference certificate, if present.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_CMP_MSG_read
loads a DER-encoded OSSL_CMP_MSG from
.Fa file .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_CMP_MSG_write
stores the given OSSL_CMP_MSG to
.Fa file
in DER encoding.
.Pp
.Fn d2i_OSSL_CMP_MSG_bio
parses an ASN.1-encoded OSSL_CMP_MSG from the BIO
.Fa bio .
It assigns a pointer to the new structure to
.Em *msg
if
.Fa msg
is not NULL.
.Pp
.Fn i2d_OSSL_CMP_MSG_bio
writes the OSSL_CMP_MSG
.Fa msg
in ASN.1 encoding to BIO
.Fa bio .
.Sh NOTES
CMP is defined in RFC 4210.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn OSSL_CMP_MSG_get0_header
returns the intended pointer value as described above or NULL if the
respective entry does not exist and on error.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_CMP_MSG_get_bodytype
returns the body type or -1 on error.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_CMP_MSG_get0_certreq_publickey
returns a public key or NULL on error.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_CMP_CTX_setup_CRM
returns a pointer to a
.Vt OSSL_CRMF_MSG
on success, NULL on error.
.Pp
.Fn d2i_OSSL_CMP_MSG_bio
returns the parsed message or NULL on error.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_CMP_MSG_read
and
.Fn d2i_OSSL_CMP_MSG_bio
return the parsed CMP message or NULL on error.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_CMP_MSG_write
returns the number of bytes successfully encoded or a negative value if
an error occurs.
.Pp
.Fn i2d_OSSL_CMP_MSG_bio ,
.Fn OSSL_CMP_MSG_update_transactionID ,
and
.Fn OSSL_CMP_MSG_update_recipNonce
return 1 on success, 0 on error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr OSSL_CMP_CTX_set1_subjectName 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_CMP_CTX_set1_p10CSR 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_CMP_CTX_set1_oldCert 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_CMP_CTX_set0_newPkey 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_CMP_CTX_set1_pkey 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_CMP_CTX_set0_reqExtensions 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_CMP_CTX_push1_subjectAltName 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_CMP_CTX_push0_policy 3
.Sh HISTORY
The OpenSSL CMP support was added in OpenSSL 3.0.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_CMP_MSG_update_recipNonce
was added in OpenSSL 3.0.9.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_CMP_MSG_get0_certreq_publickey
was added in OpenSSL 3.3.
